{
  "summary": "Reported: Aisha Khan (HR Generalist, user_id 5) says Outlook has stopped applying her inbox rules that sort mail into folders, starting about a week ago. P3, she can still work. Checked: account is active, no lockout and no failed sign-ins. Mailbox is 24.4% used (12.5 of 50 GB), so a full mailbox is not the cause. Laptop BL-LT-0105 (Win 11) is online, checked in recently, has 47% disk free and no warnings. No KB article covers inbox rules: KB-009/010/011 don't match and a KB search found nothing relevant. Still needed: look at her mailbox rules server-side (rules disabled or in error, rule quota reached, client-only rules, rules that conflict or have 'stop processing more rules' set). Find out whether the rules run in Outlook on the web. Check for recent Outlook or policy changes. Also, since rules changed unexpectedly, confirm there are no unfamiliar forwarding or redirect rules.",
  "reason": "No KB article covers Outlook inbox rules not applying; per process, escalate instead of troubleshooting from general knowledge"
}
